{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A three-year-old she-goat.</b> Some say three goats, and what is right in my eyes is a daughter of three years." "<b>And a ram.</b> It is the large sheep." "<b>And a pigeon.</b> A young dove, for from these alone of those mentioned in animal and bird are the burnt offerings and every offering."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:38.951524664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}